🚀 Top Docker Interview Questions (Super Simple Answers)
🔹 1. What is a Container?
 A lightweight package that includes code + dependencies so apps run the same everywhere.
🔹 2. How do you create a Docker image?
 Write a Docker file → run: docker build -t my -image .
🔹 3. What is Docker Swarm?
 A tool to manage and run containers across multiple machines.
🔹 4. What is Docker Prune?
 Cleans unused containers, images, networks.
 docker system prune
🔹 5. What is Docker Commit?
 Creates a new image from a running container’s current state.
🔹 6. What is Docker Compose?
 Runs multi-container apps using a docker-compose.yml file.
🔹 7. What is EXPOSE in Docker file?
 Shows which port a container will listen on.
🔹 8. How to list Docker networks?
 docker network ls
🔹 9. COPY vs ADD
 COPY: Copies files.
 ADD: COPY + URL support + auto extract tar.
🔹 10. ENTRYPOINT vs CMD
 ENTRYPOINT: Main command.
 CMD: Default arguments.
🔹 11. What is a Dockerfile?
 A file with instructions to build an image.
🔹 12. Init vs Runtime Container (K8s)
 Init: Runs first for setup.
 Runtime: Runs the actual app.
🔹 13. How to count images?
 docker images -q | wc -l
🔹 14. How to login into a running container?
 docker exec -it <container_id> /bin/bash
🔹 15. How to check number of images?
 docker images
